 ```
 
-These run against local test fixtures, not a real merchant account.
+Do not expose the Payoneer access token in browser JavaScript, HTML, GitHub, screenshots or client-side environment variables.
+
+## How payment confirmation works
+
+1. The customer signs in, adds digital patterns and opens **International Card Payment**.
+2. The store creates a server-side order from database prices and sends a Payoneer payment-request request.
+3. The customer is redirected to the provider URL. Card details stay on the provider side.
+4. `success.html?order=...` polls the order endpoint. For Payoneer orders, the server re-checks the payment request and validates the order reference, amount and currency.
+5. When Payoneer returns a payment ID plus a paid timestamp/status indicating the payment is on its way/completed, the server atomically marks the order paid and grants only the purchased pattern files.
+6. The admin order screen also has **Sync Payoneer status**. A password-protected **Confirm verified payment** fallback exists only for cases where API status is unavailable; use it only after matching the payment in your Payoneer dashboard.
+
+## Withdrawals
+
+Money received through an eligible Payoneer service is managed in Payoneer. This application does **not** ask for or store your Payoneer card details and does not fake a withdrawal API. `PAYOUT_MODE=request` records internal payout notes only; complete real withdrawals in the Payoneer dashboard to your supported bank account.
+
+## Digital-product checkout fields
+
+The website intentionally does not ask for a shipping/street address. The checkout UI contains:
+
+- International Card Payment
+- Cardholder Name
+- Card Number — entered on Payoneer's secure page
+- Expiry Date — entered on Payoneer's secure page
+- CVV — entered on Payoneer's secure page
+- Phone Number with country code
+- Country (full country list)
+- Province / State
+- City
+- ZIP / Postal code
+
+## Before live launch
+
+Use only Payoneer credentials issued for your approved integration. Confirm that your Payoneer account supports the store currency you configured. Run a sandbox purchase, verify the provider status updates the order to `paid`, verify only the purchased PDF unlocks, test a cancelled/failed payment, test duplicate status checks, and confirm your production HTTPS origin before accepting real money.
+
+Official references used while implementing this build:
 
-References: [Safepay Express Checkout](https://safepay-docs.netlify.app/build-your-integration/express-checkout/), [webhook verification](https://safepay-docs.netlify.app/developers/webhooks/verify-hmac-signatures/), [webhook events](https://safepay-docs.netlify.app/developers/webhooks/webhook-types/), [ISO country codes](https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html).
+- Payoneer Checkout: https://www.payoneer.com/checkout/
+- Payoneer Billing Services / Payment Requests: https://www.payoneer.com/developers-docs/accounts-receivable/ar-billing-services/
+- Payoneer developer/API access is subject to account eligibility and onboarding.
